config VIDEO_OWL_S900
	bool "Actions Semi S900 display engine with HDMI output"
	depends on VIDEO && MACH_S900 && CLK && DM_RESET && OF_LIBFDT
	help
	  Drives the S900 display engine path 0 into the HDMI transmitter
	  at a 1080p or 720p CEA mode, scanning out a 1920x1080 XRGB8888
	  framebuffer at 0x19000000 that the display engine scales to the
	  output, as the vendor U-Boot 2015.07 does. With DM_I2C the mode
	  is the best one the sink's EDID lists, read over the I2C bus the
	  display node's ddc-i2c-bus names; the bg96_hdmi_mode environment
	  variable can name one instead, and bg96_hdmi selects auto, force
	  or off. The board's ft_board_setup() hands the framebuffer to the
	  OS as a simple-framebuffer.
